Fixed. The bug: `foodSurplus >= 0` was causing the population to increase even when production was equal to consumption (surplus of 0). Changed it to `> 0`. Tests pass, and type checking passes too.
Fixed. The bug was in src/sim.ts:43 — the growth check was `if (foodSurplus >= 0)`, so a settlement producing exactly as much food as it consumes (surplus of 0) still grew its population by 1 every turn, compounding into endless growth. Changed it to `if (foodSurplus > 0)` so population only grows on a genuine surplus.

Verified: `npm run test` (4/4 passing) and `npm run typecheck` both clean.


